TABULARIUM
LICENSING, THIRD-PARTY MATERIALS, AND SOURCE-FIDELITY NOTICE

This file has two parts:

Part I  — project-specific scope and notices for Tabularium.
Part II — the Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal legal code.

Part I defines the material to which Tabularium applies CC0 and the material
that is excluded. Part I does not modify the CC0 legal code in Part II.


PART I — TABULARIUM-SPECIFIC SCOPE AND NOTICES

1. Project nature

Tabularium is an independent, unofficial, source-faithful corpus of primary
public financial, corporate, statistical, and institutional publications.
Its purpose is to preserve primary-source material and machine-readable
representations of that material for archival, research, computational, and
other downstream uses.


2. CC0-covered Tabularium contributions

To the extent that Tabularium contributors hold the relevant copyright,
database rights, or related rights, original Tabularium contributions are
dedicated to the public domain under the Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal
Public Domain Dedication.

CC0-covered original contributions may include, where independently created
by Tabularium contributors:

- repository structure, routing, and organisation;
- original metadata, cataloguing, and classification;
- original documentation;
- manifests, indexes, and registries;
- original schemas, machine-readable markup, and other project-created
  material, to the extent that such material is independently protected and
  does not merely reproduce third-party source content; and
- other original material explicitly identified as a Tabularium contribution.

For purposes of Part II below, the "Work" to which Tabularium applies CC0
means only the CC0-covered original contributions described above, together
with any other material explicitly marked as CC0. It does not mean the entire
contents of this repository.


3. Third-party source materials are excluded

Tabularium contains or may contain documents, datasets, spreadsheets,
financial statements, statistical releases, reports, publications, images,
and other materials originating from governments, public institutions,
exchanges, companies, organisations, and other third parties.

Those third-party materials are not relicensed or dedicated to the public
domain by Tabularium under CC0.

When a Tabularium artifact reproduces, transcribes, converts, reformats, or
otherwise represents a third-party publication, the source-derived content
remains excluded from the Tabularium CC0 dedication. To the extent that such
an artifact also contains separable, independently protected original
contributions created by Tabularium contributors, only those original
contributions are covered by CC0.

Any copyright, database rights, neighbouring rights, contractual restrictions,
or other rights applicable to third-party materials remain with their
respective rightsholders or are governed by applicable law and the terms of
the original source.

The inclusion of material in Tabularium does not represent or imply that
Tabularium owns that material, has authority to license it, has cleared all
rights in it, or has determined that it is in the public domain.

Some third-party materials may be in the public domain, may not qualify for
copyright protection, or may otherwise be freely reusable under applicable
law. Other materials may remain protected. Tabularium makes no blanket
determination regarding the legal status of every archived item.


4. Machine-assisted processing and source fidelity

Some machine-readable representations in Tabularium are created, assisted, or
validated using automated tools, including AI-based transcription, extraction,
format conversion, table reconstruction, classification, and validation.
Human processing may also be involved.

Tabularium aims to preserve the meaning, reported values, units, periods,
structure, and provenance of the originating publication. Nevertheless,
machine-assisted or human conversion may introduce accidental discrepancies
from the primary source. Such discrepancies may include, without limitation:

- omitted, duplicated, or substituted text;
- character or digit substitutions;
- incorrect signs, decimal separators, percentages, dates, or units;
- row/column or period misalignment in tables;
- omitted or misplaced notes, footnotes, labels, or headings;
- formatting loss; or
- incorrect structural reconstruction.

Source-faithful representation is a methodological objective of Tabularium,
not a warranty of perfect textual, numerical, structural, or semantic
equivalence with the originating publication.

Any accidental discrepancy is an error in the Tabularium representation. It
does not amend, correct, supersede, supplement, or reinterpret the originating
source.

Where a Tabularium representation conflicts with the originating publication
or a preserved native source artifact, the originating source is authoritative.
Users should independently verify information that is important, material, or
decision-relevant against the originating publication or source artifact.


5. Provenance and source availability

Tabularium aims to preserve sufficient provenance to identify the originating
institution, publication series, release, period, and source artifact whenever
reasonably possible.

Original source URLs may be recorded when available, but are not guaranteed to
remain available. Websites, publication systems, paths, and historical
attachments may change or disappear over time.

The absence of a working source URL does not imply ownership of the material by
Tabularium and does not alter the legal status of the material.


6. Independence and no endorsement

Tabularium is not affiliated with, sponsored by, approved by, or endorsed by
the institutions or other third parties whose public materials are preserved
or represented in this repository, unless expressly stated otherwise.

Names, marks, and other identifiers of source institutions are used for
provenance and identification purposes.


7. No professional advice; verification recommended

Tabularium is an archival and research corpus. Its contents are not investment,
legal, accounting, tax, regulatory, or other professional advice.

Users remain responsible for evaluating whether a source or representation is
suitable for their intended use. Important information should be checked
against the originating publication, especially when it may affect financial,
legal, regulatory, research, operational, or other material decisions.


8. No additional warranties

To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, Tabularium is provided on
an "as-is" and "as-available" basis. Tabularium makes no representation or
warranty regarding completeness, accuracy, currentness, availability,
non-infringement, or fitness for a particular purpose.

The CC0 legal code below contains additional limitations and disclaimers
applicable to the CC0-covered Work.


9. Other rights and software

Nothing in this file grants rights that Tabularium contributors do not hold or
have authority to grant. Rights outside the scope of CC0, including third-party
trademark, patent, privacy, publicity, personality, confidentiality, or similar
rights, may continue to apply.

Software code is not covered by the Tabularium CC0 dedication unless it is
explicitly identified as covered. Substantial software, scripts, crawlers,
parsers, validators, or other tooling may be licensed separately.


